        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Peronism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1943 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Thinkers</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-peron">Juan Perón</a> (1895–1974), its founder; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eva-peron">Eva Perón</a>, champion of migrant workers, the poor and women’s suffrage; John William Cooke, theorist of revolutionary Peronism; Augusto Vandor, union leader of “Peronism without Perón”; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-menem">Carlos Menem</a>, who turned it to free-market policies; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor-kirchner">Néstor Kirchner</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cristina-fernandez-de-kirchner">Cristina Fernández de Kirchner</a>, who returned it to the left</span></div>
